<script lang="ts">
	import { englishExamples as examples } from '../../utils/examples.en'

	const toast = useToast()
	const dismissed = signal(false)
	const loading = signal(true)
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Feedback"
		description="Alert, Toast, Empty and Skeleton: what the interface says when something happens, is missing or has not arrived yet."
	>
		<h2 id="alert">UIAlert</h2>
		<p>
			A notice inside the page, in four tones besides the neutral one.
			<code>danger</code>
			uses
			<code>role="alert"</code>; the others,
			<code>note</code>. Choose
			<code>status</code>
			to announce a change, or
			<code>none</code>
			when it is already inside a live region.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIAlert
				tone="info"
				title="New version"
				description="UI 1.8 uses the --ui-* tokens."
			/>
			<UIAlert
				tone="success"
				title="Changes saved"
				description="They are already published."
			/>
			<UIAlert
				tone="warning"
				title="Translation pending"
				description="This page is not in English yet."
			/>
			<UIAlert
				if:when="!dismissed.value"
				tone="danger"
				title="Could not publish"
				description="The database does not respond."
				dismiss
				on:dismiss="() => (dismissed.value = true)"
			>
				<snippet name="actions">
					<UIButton
						size="sm"
						variant="outline"
					>
						Retry
					</UIButton>
				</snippet>
			</UIAlert>
			<UIButton
				if:when="dismissed.value"
				variant="outline"
				on:click="() => (dismissed.value = false)"
			>
				Show the notice again
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.alert" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIAlert props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'tone', type: 'neutral | info | success | warning | danger', default: 'neutral', description: 'Meaning of the notice.' },
				{ name: 'title / description', type: 'string', description: 'Title and text.' },
				{ name: 'role', type: 'alert | status | note | none', default: 'alert with danger; note', description: 'How a screen reader announces it.' },
				{ name: 'dismiss / closeLabel', type: 'boolean / string', default: 'false', description: 'Close button, with its accessible name.' },
				{ name: 'icon', type: 'Snippet', description: 'Icon, as a prop or as a snippet.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>default</code>,
			<code>icon</code>
			and
			<code>actions</code>
			snippets, and the
			<code>dismiss</code>
			event.
		</p>
		<h2 id="toast">UIToast</h2>
		<p>
			A short notice floating over the page. It is a manual
			<code>popover</code>: it does not take the focus.
			<code>useToast()</code>
			is auto-imported and adds notices from a client action, never during SSR. It needs
			<MeekoLink to="/app">UIApp</MeekoLink>
			at the root.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIButton on:click="() => toast.add({ text: 'Changes saved', tone: 'success', duration: 5000 })">Notify the save</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="outline"
				on:click="() => toast.add({ text: 'Could not publish', tone: 'danger', duration: 0 })"
			>
				Notify an error
			</UIButton>
			<UIButton
				variant="ghost"
				on:click="() => toast.clear()"
			>
				Close all
			</UIButton>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.toast" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="toast.add options and UIToast props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'text', type: 'string', description: 'Required. The notice.' },
				{ name: 'tone', type: 'neutral | info | success | warning | danger', default: 'neutral', description: 'Meaning of the notice.' },
				{ name: 'duration', type: 'number', default: '5000', description: 'Milliseconds before it closes; 0 keeps it until it is closed. The count pauses with the pointer or the focus inside.' },
				{ name: 'closeLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Accessible name of the close button.' },
				{ name: 'actions', type: 'Snippet', description: 'Actions of the notice.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			<code>add</code>
			returns an id for
			<code>remove(id)</code>;
			<code>clear()</code>
			closes them all.
			<code>UIToast</code>
			can also be used declaratively, with the
			<code>dismiss</code>
			event.
		</p>
		<h2 id="empty">UIEmpty</h2>
		<p>
			What shows when there is nothing.
			<code>inline</code>
			for a list,
			<code>panel</code>
			for a whole view.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UIEmpty
				variant="panel"
				title="No projects"
				description="Create the first one to start."
			>
				<snippet name="actions"><UIButton>Create project</UIButton></snippet>
			</UIEmpty>
			<UIEmpty description="No filter matches." />
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIEmpty props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'title', type: 'string', default: 'No results.', description: 'Title. The default value follows the language of the document.' },
				{ name: 'description', type: 'string', description: 'What to do next.' },
				{ name: 'variant', type: 'inline | panel', default: 'inline', description: 'Size of the empty space.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>default</code>
			and
			<code>actions</code>
			snippets.
		</p>
		<h2 id="skeleton">UISkeleton</h2>
		<p>The shape of the content while it arrives. It announces the load once and respects reduced motion.</p>
		<DocsPreview layout="stack">
			<UISwitch
				label="Loading"
				model="loading"
			/>
			<UISkeleton
				if:when="loading.value"
				bind:lines="3"
				bind:widths="['full', 'long', 'short']"
			/>
			<p
				if:when="!loading.value"
				class="docs-status"
			>
				The content has arrived.
			</p>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.empty" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UISkeleton props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'lines', type: 'number', default: '3', description: 'Number of lines.' },
				{ name: 'widths', type: 'readonly (full | long | short)[]', description: 'Width of each line.' },
				{ name: 'label', type: 'string', default: 'Loading', description: 'What it announces. The default value follows the language of the document.' },
				{ name: 'class', type: 'string', description: 'Additional classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			The default texts are in
			<code>ui.messages.&lt;language&gt;.feedback</code>
			(see
			<MeekoLink to="/theming">Theming</MeekoLink>). The types
			<code>UIAlertProps</code>,
			<code>UIToastProps</code>,
			<code>UIToastContext</code>,
			<code>UIEmptyProps</code>
			and
			<code>UISkeletonProps</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/runtime</code>.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
